{"unit":"13","questions":[{"q":"5, 14, 23, 32, 41, … What is term 62?","options":["554","563","558","549"],"why":"The jump is 9. Term 62 has 61 jumps: 5 + (61 × 9) = 5 + 549 = 554.","src":"Review Q27, p.261","fig":null},{"q":"5, 14, 23, 32, 41, … What is the rule?","options":["Add 9 each time","Add 5 each time","Add 7 each time","Multiply by 3"],"why":"14 - 5 = 9, 23 - 14 = 9. The pattern adds 9 each time.","src":"Review Q27, p.261","fig":null},{"q":"1 triangle needs 3 toothpicks, 2 need 6, 3 need 9. How many toothpicks for 28 triangles?","options":["84","81","31","56"],"why":"Each triangle needs 3 toothpicks: 28 × 3 = 84.","src":"Review Q28, p.261","fig":null},{"q":"Separate toothpick triangles: 3, 6, 9, 12, … How many toothpicks for 10 triangles?","options":["30","27","33","13"],"why":"10 × 3 = 30.","src":"Review Q28, p.261","fig":null},{"q":"Circles in rows of 1, 3, 5, …: Figure 1 = 1, Figure 2 = 4, Figure 3 = 9. Figure 65?","options":["4,225","2,120","3,225","130"],"why":"Square numbers: 65 × 65 = 4,225.","src":"p.215","fig":null},{"q":"4, 10, 16, 22, 28, … What is term 38?","options":["226","232","228","222"],"why":"The jump is 6. Term 38 has 37 jumps: 4 + (37 × 6) = 4 + 222 = 226.","src":"p.216","fig":null},{"q":"What is the sum of all even numbers smaller than 100?","options":["2,450","2,550","2,500","2,352"],"why":"24 pairs of 98 = 2,352, plus 98 left over = 2,450.","src":"p.217","fig":null},{"q":"How many even numbers are smaller than 100?","options":["49","50","48","51"],"why":"50 even numbers from 1 to 100, but 100 itself is not smaller than 100: 50 - 1 = 49.","src":"p.217","fig":null},{"q":"Peter's toothpicks: 1, 4, 7, 10, … How many in Figure 5?","options":["13","14","16","12"],"why":"Add 3 each time: 10 + 3 = 13.","src":"p.219 (a)","fig":null},{"q":"Peter's toothpicks: 1, 4, 7, 10, … How many in Figure 10?","options":["28","31","30","27"],"why":"1 + (9 × 3) = 1 + 27 = 28.","src":"p.219 (b)","fig":null},{"q":"Henry's toothpick triangles: 3, 5, 7, 9, … H