× 4) = 1 + 36 = 37.","src":"Let's Think Along (b), p.225","fig":null},{"q":"John had 100 baht and saved 40 baht more each day until he had 420 baht. How many days?","options":["8","10","11","7"],"why":"420 - 100 = 320, and 320 ÷ 40 = 8.","src":"Problem Solving, p.227","fig":null},{"q":"Square patterns: 1, 4, 9, 16, … How many in Figure 100?","options":["10,000","1,000","200","400"],"why":"100 × 100 = 10,000.","src":"Math Journal, p.229","fig":null},{"q":"Dean has 50 baht, then saves 30 baht each day from Day 2. How much on Day 10?","options":["320 baht","350 baht","300 baht","800 baht"],"why":"50 + (9 × 30) = 50 + 270 = 320 baht.","src":"Math in Real Life, p.230","fig":null},{"q":"3, 7, 11, 15, … What is term 10?","options":["39","43","40","35"],"why":"Add 4 each time: 3 + (9 × 4) = 3 + 36 = 39.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"2, 7, 12, 17, … What is term 20?","options":["97","102","100","95"],"why":"Add 5 each time: 2 + (19 × 5) = 2 + 95 = 97.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"7, 10, 13, 16, … What is term 30?","options":["94","97","90","100"],"why":"Add 3 each time: 7 + (29 × 3) = 7 + 87 = 94.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"6, 15, 24, 33, … What is term 12?","options":["105","114","108","99"],"why":"Add 9 each time: 6 + (11 × 9) = 6 + 99 = 105.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"How many jumps are there from term 1 to term 45?","options":["44","45","46","90"],"why":"The jumps are always 1 less than the term number: 45 - 1 = 44.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"Which number pattern adds 7 each time?","options":["4, 11, 18, 25","7, 14, 21, 29","4, 11, 17, 24","1, 7, 49, 343"],"why":"11 - 4 = 7, 18 - 11 = 7, 25 - 18 = 7.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"Peter's toothpick squares: 1, 4, 7, 10, … Which Figure uses 31 toothpicks?","options":["Figure 11","Figure 10","Figure 31","Figure 12"],"why":"31 - 1 = 30, 30 ÷ 3 = 10 groups, so it is Figure 10 + 1 = Figure 11.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"10, 20, 30, 40, … What is term 15?","options":["150","140","160","25"],"why":"10 + (14 × 10) = 10 + 140 = 150.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"Square numbers: 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, … What is the 12th square number?","options":["144","24","121","132"],"why":"12 × 12 = 144.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"Lily saves 20 baht on Day 1 and 15 baht more each day after. How much does she have on Day 8?","options":["125 baht","140 baht","120 baht","160 baht"],"why":"20 + (7 × 15) = 20 + 105 = 125 baht.","src":"New","fig":null},{"q":"1 + 2 + 3 + … + 20 = ? (Pair them: 1 + 20, 2 + 19, …)","options":["210","200","420","220"],"why":"10 pairs of 21: 10 × 21 = 210.","src":"New","fig":null}]}